# Copy this file to .env (which is gitignored) and fill in real values.
# Never commit .env itself.
#
# Twilio credentials, used by:
#   - core/agents/manager_agent.py's place_call()   (voice calls - Phase 2)
#   - core/services/twilio_verify.py                (passenger OTP - Phase 3)
#
# Without these four set, both fall back to a simulated mode: place_call()
# logs what it would have said instead of dialling, and twilio_verify.py
# accepts the code "000000" instead of texting a real one. That's normal for
# local dev - fill these in only when testing against real Twilio.
#
# One-time setup before OTP verification can go live:
#   1. In the Twilio Console, verify/buy a phone number -> TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER.
#   2. Console -> Verify -> Services -> Create new Service (or
#      client.verify.v2.services.create(friendly_name="RailBot BD") via API).
#      Copy the resulting SID (starts with "VA") -> TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID.
#
# Trial-account note: Verify SMS and voice calls can only reach numbers you
# have verified in the Console first - same restriction as the Phase 2 calls.

TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=
TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID=
